title: Federated wiki records when and whence a page was forked; skg records neither, so a fork holds no baseline of its own.
pid: 64be5f84-de63-4e20-83ef-6d527e795067
body: |2-
  Its client shows a page's "twins", the pages of the same title on
  other sites it knows of, binned newer, same or older by comparing
  each one's last edit date with this page's last edit that was not a
  fork, up to eight flags a bin. That one signal, newer or not, with no
  count and no diff, is all a system built wholly on forking showed of
  other copies for a decade. skg's perspective switch already does the
  better half of twins, by ID instead of title: it cycles among the
  authors whose forks would change the buffer. What skg lacks is
  "newer": 'build_fork_clone' records no time and no state of the
  original, and no node in skg has a date ('RelPartner' is a relRepo and
  a member; checked 2026-11-15). The action that would mend it:
  [[id:52dfce32-ca0f-45fe-8b09-e24e083536c8][Record, in each fork, a fingerprint of the original it copied.]]
